		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=25442#p25442"><![CDATA[
I planned to spend this sunday on a game I started but left gathering dust for a while, for my surprise one of its dependencies (Bullet) has a new version <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"> <br><br>I haven't seen the new features added since the version I started using, but I did try the premake build system and is very easy to use; I just unzipped the file then when to the <strong class="text-strong">bullet-2.79\msvc\vs2010</strong> folder, then opened the <strong class="text-strong">0BulletSolution</strong> file, waited for VS to parse the files and then build, very easy!! <br><br>Thanks Erwin and all the guys who collaborated on this release.<br><br>EDIT: The premake files did not build the BulletMultiThreaded lib, so I had to use CMake for that. Anyway premake is cool <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_wink.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=";)" title="Wink"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5410">jomunoz</a> — Sun Sep 18, 2011 1:58 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
